for anyone who may not know: 

Chuseok is a three day long harvest festival that takes place on the 15th day of the 8th month of the lunar calendar. 🍁🎑 since it goes by the lunar calendar, the actual date(s) on the Gregorian calendar may vary, but it's usually around the end of September or early October. many people call Chuseok "Korean Thanksgiving" given that they celebrate the harvest with a big feast and large family gatherings are a major part of it. it's also common for people to give worship to their ancestors during Chuseok, and they might even make their departed ones' favorite meals as offerings. ❤ 

you may also hear people refer to this holiday as Hangawi or Jungchujeol. this year, Chuseok falls on September 28th through September 30th. 추석 잘 보내세요 (have a good Chuseok!) 🌙❤
